<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil advances, demand hesitant.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil advances, demand hesitant.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.8285)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     34.00/34.70     18.59/18.97   33.80/34.20</p>
<p> BREMEN		34.00/34.70     18.59/18.97   33.80/34.20</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    34.60/35.00     18.92/19.14   34.10/34.50</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   35.20/35.70     19.25/19.52   34.80/35.20</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   35.40/35.80     19.36/19.57   34.90/35.30</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  36.80/37.20     20.12/20.34   36.40/36.80</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were marked up by around 50 pfennigs. The dollar remains sturdy at over 1.82 marks in Europe, continuing to stifle inland demand. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
